logs/

# BOB-219 (partial — see docs/qa/BOB-219/closure_evidence_20260923.md for
# the full honest-boundary note): docs/qa/**/*.log above only rescues the
# *.log deny above it — a QA-evidence file caught by a DIFFERENT deny
# pattern elsewhere in this file (e.g. a captured `loginctl_user_state.txt`,
# matched by *_user*) is STILL silently swallowed despite living under
# docs/qa/. A blanket `!docs/qa/**` was TRIED and REJECTED in review
# (§11.4.201(1)): measured on a scratch `docs/qa/FAKE/.env`, it rescues a
# genuine secret file too — and a narrower re-deny of the word-substring
# globs (*credentials*/*_password*/etc.) scoped to docs/qa/** would risk
# reproducing the SAME false-null one directory down, on legitimate
# auth-testing QA evidence whose SUBJECT is credentials (this project
# authors exactly that kind of evidence routinely — e.g. BOB-198/BOB-203's
# runtime-auth-verification captures). No safe blanket fix exists yet;
# left as an explicit, tracked follow-up rather than shipped either
# under-protective or over-eager.

