# IDE directories
# '.opencode/*' not '.opencode/' — the tracked Spec Kit agent commands under
# .opencode/command/ must stay addable (git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent dir is excluded).
.opencode/*
!.opencode/command/
.specify/*
!.specify/README.md
# The rest of .specify/ is TRACKED Spec Kit governance (templates, extensions,
# scripts, integrations, manifests). Only .specify/workflows/ is generated and
# stays ignored by the blanket rule above.
!.specify/extensions/
!.specify/extensions.yml
!.specify/feature.json
!.specify/init-options.json
!.specify/integration.json
!.specify/integrations/
!.specify/scripts/
!.specify/templates/
# ...EXCEPT the vendored superspec extension checkout: it carries its OWN .git
# (gitdir pointer), ~14 MB of PNG assets, and its own .github/workflows/ CI
# file, and it DUPLICATES the root `superspec` submodule (same upstream,
# WangX0111/superspec). Committing it would create a phantom gitlink that is
# not registered in .gitmodules. Stays ignored.
#
# BOB-244 (2026-09-25): CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD flagged 4 untracked files
# under .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/ (e2e-agent-claude.sh,
# e2e-smoke.sh, validate-extension-metadata.py, validate-release-archive.py)
# as looking first-party. Investigated: all 4 are BYTE-IDENTICAL (verified
# via `diff -q`) to their counterparts already tracked under the real
# `superspec/` submodule — confirmed vendored duplicates, not first-party
# content. Classified vendored-and-correctly-ignored; `scripts/pre_build/
# check_gitignore_swallow.sh`'s EXCLUDED_PATH_PREFIXES now explicitly
# excludes this whole directory (never guess at a per-file negation here —
# the WHOLE checkout is the duplicate, per the paragraph above).
.specify/extensions/superspec/
# .specify/memory/ holds the TRACKED project constitution — authoritative
# governance source data, never a build artifact. Per §11.4.30 (tracked
# authoritative content is never gitignored) and §11.4.215 (a doc that
# BINDS work MUST live tracked in the repo where that work happens), the
# blanket .specify/* rule above must not shadow it: without this negation
# `git add .specify/memory/constitution.md` exits non-zero and breaks the
# §11.4.234 commit/push mechanism (always-unblocked invariant).
!.specify/memory/

