# CodeGraph (§11.4.78/§11.4.80) — local semantic index DB is a build artifact.
# Regeneration mechanism (§11.4.77): `codegraph index` rebuilds it from source.
# .codegraph/config.json (if present) is TRACKED; the DB + WAL/SHM are not.
.codegraph/codegraph.db
.codegraph/*.db-wal
.codegraph/*.db-shm
.codegraph/cache/

# docs/workable_items.db itself IS tracked (§11.4.95 — it's authoritative
# source data, not a build artifact); its transient WAL-mode sidecars are not.
docs/*.db-wal
docs/*.db-shm

# CodeGraph third-party exclusion (§11.4.79): the Jackett submodule is
# third-party (Jackett/Jackett, C#/.NET) and MUST NOT enter the index.
# CodeGraph reads .gitignore directly to decide what to index; this entry is
# INERT for git (submodules/jackett is a tracked gitlink via .gitmodules, so
# git keeps tracking the submodule pointer) but tells CodeGraph to skip it.
# The own-org `constitution/` submodule (HelixDevelopment) is deliberately NOT
# listed here so it stays INCLUDED in the index per §11.4.79.
submodules/jackett/

# BOB-225 (operator decision 2026-09-23, superseding the prior "not tracked
# to avoid dozens of binary blobs" choice below): §11.4.65/§11.4.153 MANDATE
# a four-format (HTML+PDF+DOCX) export for every in-scope Markdown document.
# A deny-all *.docx glob with only a 2-file allowlist meant 1138 of 1140
# generated DOCX twins on disk were untracked-and-invisible (git status
# silent, the exact BOB-212-class false-null) — including the exact two
# tracked survivors (docs/features/Status.docx/_Summary.docx) being alive
# only by accident of already being in the index, one delete-and-re-add
# from vanishing the same way. VERIFIED 2026-09-23: every one of the 384
# docs/**/*.docx + 7 repo-root */.docx + 2 scripts/**/*.docx files on this
# checkout pairs 1:1 with a tracked .md sibling (no exceptions found) — a
# genuine export twin, never a stray/unrelated Word document.
#
# DOCX exports are generated on demand (regen: scripts/generate_markdown_exports.sh,
# §11.4.77) — not hand-authored. The deny-all glob is KEPT (a hand-authored
# or third-party .docx landing anywhere else in the tree is still refused
# by default); only genuine generated-twin locations are carved out.
*.docx
!docs/**/*.docx
!scripts/**/*.docx
!README.docx
!AGENTS.docx
!CLAUDE.docx
!QWEN.docx
!CONTRIBUTING.docx
!CONSTITUTION.docx
!CHANGELOG.docx

