scratchpad/

# Subagent-Driven-Development coordination ledgers (§11.4.30 temp-file class).
# Per-plan scratch: ledger, task briefs, implementer reports, review packages.
# Deliberately NOT tracked — the binding record is the evidence pack under
# docs/qa/ plus git history (§11.4.215: a doc that BINDS work lives tracked;
# this one only coordinates, so it does not). Kept in-repo rather than in the
# session scratchpad because the scratchpad path is keyed to the session id,
# so a session restart orphans it — which is exactly the failure this ledger
# exists to prevent.
.superpowers/

# §11.4.10 CRITICAL (operator mandate 2026-08-15) — cookies txt files
# MUST NEVER be git-versioned. Convention: ~/Downloads/cookies_<TRACKER>.txt
# is the DEFAULT external source; the file itself should live OUTSIDE the repo,
# but this pattern also guards against accidental drops of the file INTO the tree.
cookies_*.txt
**/cookies_*.txt
.cookies/
tracker-cookies/

# Export-pipeline scratch files (§11.4.30 temp-file class).
# The PDF exporter writes `toPdfViaTempFile<pid>-<n>.{html,pdf}` into the
# REPO ROOT while rendering, then removes them. Two ways they survive: the
# exporter is killed mid-render, or something reads the tree while a render
# is in flight. Observed 2026-08-21 with two generations live during a single
# `workable-items-export.sh` run. `*.tmp` (line 70) does NOT match them —
# they end in `-0.html` / `-1.pdf` — so without this pattern a `git add -A`
# concurrent with an export commits them (the §11.4.84 sweep hazard, with a
# build artifact as the payload).
toPdfViaTempFile*
